WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:22.500
Type I covers small appliances. Don't underestimate this section — it has tricky
questions.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:45.000
Type I recovery requirements: 90 percent recovery for operating systems, 80
percent for non-operating systems. Both self-contained and system-dependent
recovery equipment can be used. System-dependent recovery uses the appliance own

00:00:45.000 --> 00:01:07.500
Here are the key terms. Write these down.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:30.000
Self-Contained Recovery: Uses its own compressor to pull refrigerant out of the
system.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:52.500
System-Dependent Recovery: Uses the appliance own compressor or pressure to push
refrigerant out.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:02:15.000
Here's why this matters on the job: Proper recovery technique prevents EPA
violations and environmental damage.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:37.500
Watch out for these: 90 percent for operating, 80 percent for non-operating. And
— System-dependent relies on the appliance compressor working

00:02:37.500 --> 00:03:00.000
What is the maximum charge that defines a small appliance under EPA 608? That
number is on the exam.

